  <sys:String x:Key="Field.LoadSafetyFactor">Load limit factor</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Field.LoadSafetyFactor.Desc">Load limit = device load range x factor (100 kN → 95 kN); falls back to 50 kN when the range is unknown.</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Field.MinBreakLoad">Min. break load</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Field.MinBreakLoad.Desc">Peak load below this value is not judged as a break (factory bending constant BREAK_MIN_LOAD_KN; site value 200 N = 0.2 kN). 0 = no lower limit.</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Field.ContinueLoadingTime">Continue after break</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Field.ContinueLoadingTime.Desc">Seconds of extra loading after the break is confirmed, so the curve shows the falling trend. This part IS recorded. Then the table resets. 0 = reset right away.</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Field.EnableOriginCorrection">Origin correction</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Field.EnableOriginCorrection.Desc">Whether to correct the curve origin (some tests need it, some not). When off, origin = 0 and the strain uses the uncorrected deflection.</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Field.OriginCorrectionStart">Fit range start</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Field.OriginCorrectionStart.Desc">Start of the load range used to fit the tangent line (% of peak load). Not fixed by the standard; code default 10, site value 20.</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Field.OriginCorrectionEnd">Fit range end</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Field.OriginCorrectionEnd.Desc">End of the load range used to fit the tangent line (% of peak load). Code default 80, site value 60.</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Field.LockDisplacement">Lock peak displ.</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Field.LockDisplacement.Desc">Midspan deflection taken at the peak load point (factory LockDisplacement); selected by default. Clear it to use the maximum deflection.</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Field.LoadRate">Load rate</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Field.LoadRate.Desc">Loading rate of the test. T0715 specifies 50 mm/min ±5; motor cap 50 mm/min. Site value is 5.</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Field.ContactLoad">Contact load</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Field.ContactLoad.Desc">Load above this value means the head has touched the specimen (factory ZeroDisplacement). On contact the deflection is zeroed and the rate switches to the test rate.</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Field.BreakDrop">Break drop</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Field.BreakDrop.Desc">Load falling this far below the peak counts as a break (factory PressureDrop; site value 0.5 kN).</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Field.BreakConfirmSamples">Break frames</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Field.BreakConfirmSamples.Desc">Consecutive frames required to confirm a break (factory NumberOfFilters; site value 5).</sys:String>
